+# Task M4-C2 — Correct `src/host/m4-proof.ts` for the M4 cycle-1 review findings
+
+Tier: Cheap
+Reason routed here: none of the four escalation reasons applies. Clearly specified
+(three precisely-named edits, all in one file, all stated below), bounded (one file),
+low risk (the file is a proof script, not production code; no `web/src/` behaviour
+changes), easily verified (`bun run proof:m4` must still exit 0 with all three
+criteria PASS, and `bun test` must still be 253 pass / 0 fail).
+
+## Review report
+
+`/Users/ryankenny/Projects/phoneToLocalModel/.harness/reviews/M4-cycle1.md`.
+Read it for context. You are correcting the IMPORTANT finding (partially — the
+rest of it is a record change the orchestrator makes) and the first OPTIONAL
+finding. Do NOT act on the second OPTIONAL finding (timing sensitivity); the
+orchestrator has explicitly declined it.
+
+## Established fact you must not re-investigate
+
+A separate, already-completed and independently-verified probe (task `M4-C1`)
+established against the LIVE API that a generation CANNOT be driven to a terminal
+`failed` status: every malformed request is rejected at the HTTP layer with a 4xx
+and no generation id is ever created.
+
+  POST with a nonexistent profile_id -> HTTP 400 `{"api_version":"v1","error":"unknown_profile"}`
+  POST with an empty prompt          -> HTTP 400 `{"api_version":"v1","error":"invalid_request"}`
+  POST to a nonexistent session      -> HTTP 404 `{"api_version":"v1","error":"unknown_session"}`
+
+No `x-generation-id` header and no generation id in any body. The only remaining
+routes to a `failed` generation are `inference_failed` (requires the backend
+inference to fail — no client-side lever) and `generation_timed_out` (a 300s wait,
+out of budget).
+
+**Do NOT attempt to induce a failed generation. Do NOT add a sub-case for it.**
+The correction is to disclose the gap honestly, not to close it.
+
+## Context
+
+- Repo root: `/Users/ryankenny/Projects/phoneToLocalModel`
+- Bun 1.4.0 is at `~/.bun/bin/bun` and is NOT on PATH in non-interactive shells.
+  Export `PATH="$HOME/.bun/bin:$PATH"`. Node is not installed; do not reach for it.
+- `bun run proof:m4` runs against the LIVE harness and takes ~30-60s.
+- The harness has a SINGLE generation slot. If a run fails part-way it can wedge
+  that slot; the script already has a `lastAdmitted` / `releaseIfStuck` safety net.
+  Do not remove or bypass it.
+
+## The three edits
+
+### Edit 1 — disclose the untested `failed` sub-case (IMPORTANT finding)
+
+In the PHASE 2 header comment block (currently at lines 224-225, immediately above
+the `console.log("\n=== PHASE 2: ...")` call), add a clearly-worded comment
+recording that this phase proves the idempotency contract for TWO of the three
+terminal states the requirement names, and why the third is absent. It must state,
+in your own clear prose:
+
+- the requirement names three terminal states: already-complete, already-failed,
+  already-cancelled;
+- this phase exercises `complete` (sub-case A) and `cancelled` (sub-case B) live;
+- the already-`failed` state is NOT exercised, because a `failed` generation
+  cannot be induced from the client: malformed requests are rejected at the HTTP
+  layer with 4xx before any generation id exists (quote the three observed
+  responses above), leaving only `inference_failed` (no client-side lever) and
+  `generation_timed_out` (a 300s wait);
+- the `failed` case therefore rests on the documented API contract and on the fact
+  that `cancel()` forwards the service's `status` string verbatim with no
+  per-value branching — i.e. on inference, NOT on live proof.
+
+### Edit 2 — narrow the Phase 2 PASS/FAIL wording to what is actually proven
+
+The two `console.log` lines that currently read
+
+    "Criterion 2 (idempotent cancel returns the actual final status): PASS"
+    "Criterion 2 (idempotent cancel returns the actual final status): FAIL"
+
+must be narrowed so the printed evidence does not overstate its own coverage.
+Change the parenthetical to name the two states actually exercised — e.g.
+`(idempotent cancel returns the actual final status: complete, cancelled)`.
+Keep the `: PASS` / `: FAIL` suffix EXACTLY as-is at the end of each line; it is
+the machine-visible outcome marker. Change nothing else about these two lines.
+
+### Edit 3 — make criterion 3's flag-equality assertion live (OPTIONAL finding 1)
+
+Currently both the local and the service assistant turn are selected with the
+predicate `t.role === "assistant" && t.cancelled === true`, so the later
+`localAssistantTurn.cancelled !== serviceAssistantTurn.cancelled` comparison can
+structurally never fire — it is dead.
+
+Change BOTH selections to be independent of the `cancelled` flag: select the
+assistant turn by `t.role === "assistant"` alone (both sides are single-generation
+conversations, so there is exactly one assistant turn). The flag-equality
+comparison then becomes a genuinely live assertion.
+
+Also update the two failure messages that currently say
+`"no local assistant turn with cancelled=true found"` and
+`"no service-side assistant turn with cancelled=true found"` so they no longer
+claim a `cancelled=true` predicate they no longer apply.
+
+**The criterion must not become weaker.** After this change, a service turn
+recorded with `cancelled: false` must still FAIL criterion 3 — it will now fail on
+the flag-equality comparison (with a clearer diagnostic) instead of on the
+"no matching turn" branch. Add a check, or convince yourself by reading, that
+`criterion3Passed` is still set `false` on every divergence path, including when
+either turn is missing entirely. Do not remove the content-equality assertion.
+
+## Files allowed to change
+
+- `src/host/m4-proof.ts`
+
+NOTHING else. In particular do NOT touch `web/src/session-coordinator.ts`,
+`test/web/session-coordinator.test.ts`, `package.json`, or anything under
+`.harness/`.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1 — The Phase 2 comment block discloses the untested already-`failed` state
